{"strongs": "H2557", "word": "חָמֵץ", "translit": "cha.mets", "root": "חמץ", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "that which is leavened", "definition": "חָמֵץ noun masculine Exod 13:3 that which is leavened — ֯ ׳ ח Exod 12:15 + 10 t. — forbidden at Passover Exod 12:15 ( P ), Exod 13:3 ; Exod 13:7 ( J E ), Deut 16:3 , in all sacrifices Exod 23:18 ; Exod 34:25 (both J E ); compare Amos 4:5 ; Lev 2:11 ; Lev 6:10 ( P ; apposition); exceptions are ׳ לֶחֶם ח of peace-offering Lev 7:13 ( P ), and the wave-loaves ( ׳ ח appositive) Lev 23:17 ( H ). — see RS Sem 208 OTJC 2, 345 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2876')\">BDB2876</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2557')\">H2557</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2875')\">BDB2875</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2877')\">BDB2877</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חָמֵץ</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 13:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,3)\">Exod 13:3</ref></sup> <highlightword>that which is leavened</highlightword> — <bdbheb>֯</bdbheb><bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 12:15\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(2,12,15)\">Exod 12:15</ref> + 10 t. — forbidden at Passover <ref ref=\"Exod 12:15\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(2,12,15)\">Exod 12:15</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Exod 13:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,3)\">Exod 13:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 13:7\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,7)\">Exod 13:7</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup><lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Deut 16:3\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(5,16,3)\">Deut 16:3</ref>, in all sacrifices <ref ref=\"Exod 23:18\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(2,23,18)\">Exod 23:18</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 34:25\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(2,34,25)\">Exod 34:25</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>); compare <ref ref=\"Amos 4:5\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(30,4,5)\">Amos 4:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 2:11\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(3,2,11)\">Lev 2:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 6:10\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(3,6,10)\">Lev 6:10</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>; apposition); exceptions are <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>לֶחֶם ח</bdbheb> of peace-offering <ref ref=\"Lev 7:13\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(3,7,13)\">Lev 7:13</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), and the wave-loaves (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> appositive) <ref ref=\"Lev 23:17\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(3,23,17)\">Lev 23:17</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('H')\"><reflink>H</reflink></lookup>). — see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('RS')\">RS<sup>Sem 208 OTJC 2, 345</sup></lookup>. </p><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Exod 13:3", "book": "EXO", "chapter": 13, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Exod 12:15", "book": "EXO", "chapter": 12, "verse": 15}, {"raw": "Exod 13:7", "book": "EXO", "chapter": 13, "verse": 7}, {"raw": "Deut 16:3", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 16, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Exod 23:18", "book": "EXO", "chapter": 23, "verse": 18}, {"raw": "Exod 34:25", "book": "EXO", "chapter": 34, "verse": 25}, {"raw": "Amos 4:5", "book": "AMO", "chapter": 4, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "Lev 2:11", "book": "LEV", "chapter": 2, "verse": 11}, {"r